From: codEx Fork Bot <codex-fork-bot@localhost>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 23:03:25 +0800
Subject: rewind: resolve drifted rewinds to the newest matching snapshot

- When the ordinal mapping (nth + 1) misses, the resolver now picks the
  newest snapshot carrying the selected prompt instead of the numerically
  closest one. Resumed threads restart transcript ordinals while the
  snapshot chain continues, so the closest index can point at an older
  snapshot with the same prompt text; the newest match is the state right
  before the selected message.
- Conversation rewinds that fail to resolve in the current thread's chain
  now fall back to the workspace-wide store: a rewind fork replays older
  messages that only have snapshots in the parent conversation, and the
  repeated-rewind case would previously report no matching snapshot (or
  restore nothing) instead of restoring the parent snapshot.
- Adds regression tests for repeated rewind chains (parent-snapshot
  fallback) and for newest-match resolution over closer older matches.
